@startuml
!theme plain
|a_default| Default
|a_default|
start
:join the team and agree on the team's domain;
:create a process model and check it;
:is the process model NOT OK;
:assign negative points;
:is the process model still NOT OK;
:assign negative points again;
:can continue with the process;
:are there any issues;
:fix them in the next session and extend the process to levels 2 and 3;
:need to check the process and assign points;
:continue with the process;
:need to analyze the field of study;
:assign roles in the team;
:continue with the process and perform work according to your assigned role;
:check the progress and consult any problems that arise;
:is the project accepted;
:v1: project accepted first check ({Yes, No}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v1 = 'Yes'])
:present it;
else ([v1 = 'No'])
:continue working according to your role;
endif
:is the project accepted again;
:v2: project accepted second check ({Yes, No}); <<objectSignal>>
if () then ([v2 = 'Yes'])
:finally present the project and the process will come to an end;
else ([v2 = 'No'])
:continue working according to your role;
endif
stop
@enduml